---
/* Open Bay Rule — design system §3.2, signature option 01.
   A hairline interrupted by a real doorway: lintel, two jambs, and the 45°
   outward flap in the brand red. The door gap is the semantic core — a bay you
   can walk into — so the line is genuinely broken, not bridged.

   Deliberately NOT an SVG: a viewBox scales its 1px hairline with the drawing,
   so the door is a fixed-width <span> flex child between two flex-1 rule
   segments and the hairline stays 1px at any container width.

   Decorative only — aria-hidden, no text, no JS of its own. The one-shot
   "door opens" move is pure CSS driven by the site's existing [data-reveal]
   IntersectionObserver (src/scripts/app.js:24); see components.css §22 for the
   reduced-motion handling. */
---
<div class="bay-rule" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="bay-rule__line"></span>
  <span class="bay-rule__door">
    <span class="bay-rule__lintel"></span>
    <span class="bay-rule__jamb bay-rule__jamb--l"></span>
    <span class="bay-rule__jamb bay-rule__jamb--r"></span>
    <span class="bay-rule__flap"></span>
  </span>
  <span class="bay-rule__line"></span>
</div>
